-- ownership: one write at the end of a long written field path
-- (ownership-v2.md §2.8, §4.4 *holder and callee path words*, #1225). Each
-- step of the path is its own atom: its escape, candidates, anchors and use
-- queries go on that step's direct-demand-query lane, never the demand's
-- one lane. There is one write and no product; each declaration checks.
